.nh
.TH "PB-POLICY-EXPLAIN" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-policy-explain - Explain who can do what under the policy


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb policy explain [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Explain an access decision. With --src, --dst and --action, print whether it
is allowed, the reason and the rules that decided it. With --dst and --action
only, list who can do it; with --src only, list what that user can do. --file
explains a draft instead of the saved policy and --api-token narrows the answer
to one of your API tokens. Members can explain their own access; owners and
admins anyone's.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--action\fP=""
	the action, such as exec or private_access

.PP
\fB--api-token\fP=""
	narrow the answer to one of your API tokens, by name

.PP
\fB--dst\fP=""
	what: machine:<alias>, preview:<name>, tunnel:<name>, tag:<tag>

.PP
\fB--file\fP=""
	explain a draft policy file instead of the saved policy

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for explain

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--port\fP=0
	the port, for private_access

.PP
\fB--src\fP=""
	who: user:<email>


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb policy explain --src user:ana@example.test --dst machine:db --action private_access --port 5432
  pb policy explain --dst machine:db --action exec
  pb policy explain --src user:ana@example.test --file draft.hujson
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-policy(1)\fP
